{
  "_name_note": "Sandbox Bob is not a Bob. He is an isolated copy run inside a software sandbox so that a hostile transmission can be fed to something disposable — Bk1 ch13, Bob, August 2133, en route. He has no record in data/bobs.json and must not get one: he is never a person the books track, and by the time we meet him Guppy has already counted twenty-four of him. Whether that is a defensible line is the subject of the blog post that ships with him.",
  "_comment": "Six frames of pixel art, same machinery as Guppy: fill-opacity against currentColor so one sprite works in phosphor or amber, rendered as merged rects rather than an image. What the books give him is a vocabulary rather than dialogue, and it is exact. Bad payload: he twirls in his chair, then leaps up, grabs his throat, falls over and goes out in a scatter of pixilation. Clean payload: he hams it up, then stands, does a little jig, bows extravagantly and disappears in a puff of smoke. He never speaks. Guppy speaks in brackets; Sandbox Bob mimes, and keeping those two channels apart is what stops him becoming a second Guppy.\n\nThe scale is the joke and has to survive: what appears on Bob's table is an actual sandbox with a miniature Bob in a miniature chair sitting in it, and his own comment on that is that he is not very mature. So the box is drawn, always, and he is small inside it.",
